const faqItems = [
  {
    q: 'Which freelance skills can earn lakhs per month in India?',
    a: 'The skills with the most room are AI integration, software and app development, data analytics, performance marketing and SEO, and UX design. Video editing, copywriting and finance support can reach the same line through several monthly retainers or a small team. On the Xflow rate card, experienced web developers, UX designers and SEO specialists list Rs 2,500 to 4,000 or more an hour. No skill promises lakhs, and most people start far below.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How many billable hours does it take to bill Rs 1 lakh a month?',
    a: 'It is simple division. At Rs 1,000 an hour it takes 100 billable hours, at Rs 2,000 it takes 50, and at Rs 3,000 it takes about 34. Billable hours are the hours a client pays for, so time spent finding clients, sending quotes and fixing revisions comes on top of that.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can a beginner earn lakhs per month from freelancing?',
    a: 'Very rarely, and not at the start. AmbitionBox lists the average starting freelancer pay at about Rs 10,000 a month, and Upwork says beginners typically charge about $10 to $25 an hour. Lakhs usually come after proof, repeat clients and a higher rate.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is Rs 1 lakh billed the same as Rs 1 lakh earned?',
    a: 'No. Upwork charges a service fee of 0% to 15% per contract (Skydo, page updated 3 November 2026), bank and currency conversion costs apply, and income tax is due on what you earn. Check the current rules on the official Income Tax and GST portals or ask a chartered accountant. This is general information, not tax advice.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the average freelancer income in India?',
    a: 'No official average exists. The data is mixed and dated: AmbitionBox shows a range of Rs 1.2 lakh to Rs 15 lakh a year (page updated 28 December 2024), and press coverage of the Economic Survey 2025-26 says around 40% of gig and platform workers earn below Rs 15,000 a month, though that number is not in the government release. Pay varies by city, client and skill.',
